- directory-default-export-missing: quickjs-directory.c:322-327 has the
  "default" module export wired up but commented out, and even restoring it
  wouldn't fully fix it -- unlike quickjs-child-process.c:597/618, quickjs-
  deep.c:1137/1156, quickjs-xml.c:911/928 (which all declare "default" via
  js_addmoduleexport *and* set it via js_setmoduleexport), quickjs-directory.c
  never calls js_addmoduleexport(ctx, m, "default") at all, so the export slot
  doesn't exist for js_setmoduleexport to fill even once uncommented.

    import Directory from 'directory';
    console.log(Directory);
    // undefined -- should be the Directory constructor

- sockets-default-export-undeclared: js_sockets_init (quickjs-
  sockets.c:3107-3111) unconditionally runs js_setmoduleexport(ctx, m,
  "default", socket_ctor) when the module is loaded as "socket", but the
  matching js_addmoduleexport(ctx, m, "default") is commented out (quickjs-
  sockets.c:3145). pre-existing (predates the 2026-07-20 dbuf_claim commit).

    import Socket from 'socket';
    console.log(Socket);
    // likely undefined or ub -- export slot was never declared

- getdents-emscripten-no-syscall: src/getdents.c:299 falls back to a raw
  `syscall(SYS_getdents64, ...)` plus a hand-rolled `struct linux_dirent64`
  cast (getdents.c:322) whenever neither a linkable getdents64()/getdents()
  nor __dietlibc__ is detected. found while bringing up the
  build/wasm32-unknown-emscripten configuration added in this session:
  Emscripten's musl-based libc has neither getdents64() nor getdents() as a
  linkable symbol (so HAVE_GETDENTS64/HAVE_GETDENTS are both unset) and
  provides no syscall() function or <linux/dirent.h>-style struct at all, so
  the fallback branch fails to compile with "implicit declaration of function
  'syscall'" and "incomplete definition of type 'struct linux_dirent64'".
  mitigated (not fixed) later in the same session by excluding 'directory'
  (and src/getdents.c) from the build entirely on WASI/Emscripten, in
  CMakeLists.txt -- so this no longer blocks the default wasm build, but the
  underlying source-level bug in getdents.c is still there for anyone who
  force-enables 'directory' on Emscripten (e.g. by overriding
  BUILTINS_NATIVE/QUICKJS_MODULES by hand). A real fix would still mean
  adding a portable opendir()/readdir()-based fallback.

    cmake -B build/wasm32-unknown-emscripten -S . \
      -DQUICKJS_BUILD_ROOT=<path-to-emscripten-built-quickjs> \
      -DQUICKJS_SOURCES_ROOT=<path-to-quickjs-source-root> \
      -DBUILTINS_NATIVE="...;directory;..."
    cmake --build build/wasm32-unknown-emscripten
    # expected: builds cleanly
    # actual: CMakeFiles/modules.dir/src/getdents.c.o fails with the two
    # errors above

- test-path-stream-preexisting-failures: tests/test_path.js's `skipSeparator()`,
  `isSeparator()`, `isin()`, `equal()`, `toArray()` tests fail, and
  `equal()`/`toArray()` additionally throw "not a function" (suggesting a
  path.js API those tests expect no longer exists under that name);
  tests/test_stream.js's `tee(): both branches independently observe every
  chunk` test also throws "not a function". These assertion failures were
  always there, just never surfaced via exit code until tinytest.js's run()
  (exported as `tests`) was fixed to call std.exit(1) on any test failure
  (tests/tinytest.js:68-75) - before that, every consumer called
  `tests({...})` fire-and-forget at module scope without awaiting the
  returned promise, and run() itself never propagated failure past its own
  console output, so the qjsm process always exited 0 regardless of how many
  assertions failed, silently passing `ctest`. Left unfixed: out of scope
  (neither path.js/stream.js nor their tests have been touched to investigate
  the "not a function" root cause).

    ctest --test-dir build/<arch> -R 'test_path|test_stream'
    # expected: both FAIL, matching the failures their own console output
    # already reports
    # actual: both FAIL (ctest correctly surfaces this now - previously both
    # reported PASSED despite printing "N out of 41 tests failed" to stdout)
